WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.810
I'd love to pivot,

2
00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:03.880
yeah, I said it,

3
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:07.180
and ask you guys a round robin of questions.

4
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:08.133
You ready?

5
00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.690
(Ginnifer laughing)

6
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:10.702
Ready.
I'm ready.

7
00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:11.535
I'm nervous, but I'm ready.

8
00:00:11.535 --> 00:00:13.080
Okay, Ginnifer, it's a rainy Sunday.

9
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.560
What are you doing?

10
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:15.710
Baking bread. Making jam.

11
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:18.970
Ooh. Oh God, that's so good.

12
00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.793
Okay, Eliza, what is your go-to indulgence these days?

13
00:00:24.671 --> 00:00:26.300
Cheese?

14
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.570
Yes. Spread it all over.

15
00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:29.664
I love cheese.

16
00:00:29.664 --> 00:00:30.610
(Maggie laughing)

17
00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.803
Maggie, what is your most used emoji?

18
00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.180
Oh, the laughing one

19
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.320
with the two tears.
Yes. Okay.

20
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:44.320
Ginnifer, who is most like their character on "Pivoting"?

21
00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.120
The author.

22
00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.220
(Ginnifer laughing)

23
00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.879
Because it is autobiographical.

24
00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:53.013
Abort mission!

25
00:00:53.013 --> 00:00:56.220
We all are terrible choices as characters on this show.

26
00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.530
That's true.
I love that,

27
00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.880
'cause that actually, like,

28
00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.560
if you tell the truth and you tell your story,

29
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.710
it's gonna be better.

30
00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:03.830
All right, Eliza,

31
00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.833
what is the most embarrassing text on your phone right now?

32
00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:12.686
Oh, maybe the last one I just sent to the girls

33
00:01:12.686 --> 00:01:13.799
(group laughing)

34
00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:14.900
About cheese.

35
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.270
I'm really just keeping with this cheese storyline

36
00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:18.530
for me, and I used to be vegan.

37
00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:20.520
So this was a whole thing.

38
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.353
I love it.

39
00:01:21.353 --> 00:01:23.840
I know life without cheese is a really hard life.

40
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.480
Okay, Maggie, have you ever ghosted someone?

41
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.660
No.
Oh, that's so nice.

42
00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.010
Okay, Ginnifer, if you had the power of invisibility,

43
00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.170
what would be the first thing you would do?

44
00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.710
I think that I would probably, I mean,

45
00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:38.940
I should probably be, like,

46
00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.240
seeing what my kids are watching

47
00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.050
on television when I'm not in the room.

48
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.090
Oh my God. That's so true.

49
00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.920
It's so true. Okay.

50
00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.260
Eliza, who is the most surprising person

51
00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.543
to slide into your DMs?

52
00:01:53.776 --> 00:01:56.195
Oh, I can't divulge that information.

53
00:01:56.195 --> 00:01:57.490
(group laughing)

54
00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:59.312
But it's always good.
I know!

55
00:01:59.312 --> 00:02:00.427
I know who it is! Just kidding.

56
00:02:00.427 --> 00:02:03.090
Oh, I know who it is!

57
00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.220
Okay, but it's someone.

58
00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:07.650
It is. Oh, it is someone.

59
00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:11.083
Maggie, who was a fun on-screen kiss?

60
00:02:12.953 --> 00:02:16.310
(Maggie groaning)

61
00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.270
I hate on-screen kissing.

62
00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.450
I know, it's so weird. We all know this.

63
00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.640
Okay, you guys all know this,

64
00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.040
and I know no one's gonna believe us,

65
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:28.040
but it's the most uncomfortable situation to be in.

66
00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:29.600
No offense, men.

67
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.893
It's true. It's not sexy.
Very un-sexy.

68
00:02:32.893 --> 00:02:34.680
It's the worst.
All right.

69
00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.218
Well, oh, okay.

70
00:02:36.218 --> 00:02:38.968
Ginnifer, when's the last time you got caught in a lie?

71
00:02:39.908 --> 00:02:42.989
Oh, the last time I got caught in a lie.

72
00:02:42.989 --> 00:02:45.000
Oh, it was recently,

73
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.060
and it was somebody gave me a gift,

74
00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.870
and I hadn't actually opened it,

75
00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.187
and then I was asked about how I used it,

76
00:02:50.187 --> 00:02:51.847
and I had to guess at what it was,

77
00:02:51.847 --> 00:02:54.570
and I was wrong.
(group laughing)

78
00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:59.090
I love that. Eliza, what's your favorite song right now?

79
00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:02.450
It's an instrumental Hermanos Gutierrez song.

80
00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.283
Yeah.
Oh wow.

81
00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.640
I was not expecting that.

82
00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.580
Okay, Maggie, has a pick-up line ever worked on you,

83
00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.363
and if so, what was it?

84
00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:15.640
People very, very rarely hit on me,

85
00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.700
number one, let's get that out of the way,

86
00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.410
and then number two,

87
00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:22.050
the ones who do do the lines, I feel like,

88
00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:27.050
or ever have, are doing it as a semi-joke,

89
00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.890
because the chance of rejection,

90
00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:32.310
you see what I'm saying, is very high,

91
00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.810
and so they put it out there,

92
00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.170
and then there's a laugh, and then it's over.

93
00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.330
Yeah. Yeah.

94
00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:40.830
I know, I can't believe no one ever asks you out, Maggie.

95
00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.240
I mean, if that just, if you don't get asked out,

96
00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.743
good luck for the rest of us.

97
00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:46.793
Okay. Last round.

98
00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.750
Ginnifer, has anyone ever recognized you,

99
00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:53.180
and you made an excuse and ran away?

100
00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.010
Oh my gosh. I used to, and you know what?

101
00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.790
I started feeling like, that is,

102
00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:01.710
I started feeling really guilty about doing that.

103
00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.300
I used to think that I was

104
00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.890
preserving privacy in some way,

105
00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.420
by denying who I was and running off,

106
00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:13.420
and then I felt like even someone asking me if I'm me

107
00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.900
is a kindness, because what they are expressing,

108
00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.440
in some ways, you are familiar,

109
00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.520
because I've probably seen something that you have done,

110
00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.700
and to that, I should be saying, "Thank you",

111
00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.830
and so to that, I now say, "Yes, it is me".

112
00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.262
Okay. Eliza, what's one thing

113
00:04:27.262 --> 00:04:30.180
you only do when you're alone?

114
00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:35.180
Oh, yeah. I mean, take a bath.

115
00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.768
I'm not doing that with other people.

116
00:04:37.768 --> 00:04:40.680
(audience laughing)

117
00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:44.110
Maggie, have you ever used a bogus excuse

118
00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.540
to get out of a date, and if so, what was it?

119
00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:49.790
Yeah, I think I once said I would go,

120
00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:51.760
'cause I don't usually do one-on-one dating.

121
00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:55.170
That's very, very rare for me. It just almost never happens.

122
00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.280
So it's always like a group of people,

123
00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.900
it was like a medical,

124
00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:02.210
I made a medical excuse to get out of the dinner.

125
00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:03.610
Okay, first of all,

126
00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.790
I love the group dating dynamic.

127
00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.330
You're right why aren't we like,

128
00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.038
what's wrong with us?
Too much pressure.

129
00:05:09.038 --> 00:05:10.490
We're here talking about friendship,

130
00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:12.400
and support, and parachuting,

131
00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.680
and we're going on dates by ourselves.

132
00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:15.610
I think you just-
Don't you think

133
00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:18.030
it kills so many birds without killing any birds,

134
00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:18.863
because you sort of,

135
00:05:18.863 --> 00:05:20.340
I need to know what my friends think anyway,

136
00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.770
so why wouldn't you just meet in a group?

137
00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:23.767
And if immediately they're like,

138
00:05:23.767 --> 00:05:25.830
"That's not gonna work for us",

139
00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.700
then you also know, and then it's done,

140
00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:28.810
and then you don't have to.

141
00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.290
This is the best screening process ever!

142
00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:32.669
You guys, I'm not kidding.

143
00:05:32.669 --> 00:05:33.502
(audience applauding)

144
00:05:33.502 --> 00:05:35.076
Let's start a movement!
Oh, we should.

145
00:05:35.076 --> 00:05:36.729
(audience applauding)

146
00:05:36.729 --> 00:05:37.562
I love this.

147
00:05:37.562 --> 00:05:40.297
Ginnifer Goodwin, Eliza Coupe, Maggie Q!

148
00:05:40.297 --> 00:05:44.447
"Pivoting" airs Thursdays at 9:30 on Fox.

149
00:05:44.447 --> 00:05:47.030
(upbeat music)

